{
  "id": "21763_usowotsuku",
  "headword": "{嘘|うそ}をつく",
  "reading": "うそをつく",
  "part_of_speech": "expression, verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to tell a lie; to lie",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to tell a lie; to lie; to say something untrue",
      "explanation": "The standard expression for telling a deliberate falsehood. Uses the verb つく in the sense of uttering or producing."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21763_usowotsuku_ex1",
      "japanese": "{嘘|うそ}をついてはいけない。",
      "english": "You must not tell lies.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21763_usowotsuku_ex2",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}は{嘘|うそ}をついているに{違|ちが}いない。",
      "english": "He must be lying.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21763_usowotsuku_ex3",
      "japanese": "{子|こ}どもの{頃|ころ}、よく{嘘|うそ}をついて{叱|しか}られた。",
      "english": "When I was a child, I often got scolded for telling lies.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21763_usowotsuku_ex4",
      "japanese": "{嘘|うそ}をつくのは{簡単|かんたん}だが、{信頼|しんらい}を{取|と}り{戻|もど}すのは{難|むずか}しい。",
      "english": "Telling a lie is easy, but regaining trust is difficult.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "The most basic and common way to say \"to lie\" in Japanese. The verb つく here is a godan verb meaning \"to utter\" (different from {付|つ}く \"to attach\" or {着|つ}く \"to arrive\"). The expression is a fixed collocation — {嘘|うそ} always takes を and つく in this meaning.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {嘘|うそ}をつく: to tell a lie\n- {嘘|うそ}をつき{通|とお}す: to keep lying, to maintain a lie\n- {大|おお}{嘘|うそ}をつく: to tell a big lie\n- {嘘|うそ}つき: liar (noun)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {嘘|うそ}も{方便|ほうべん}: the end justifies the means (proverb — even lies can be expedient)\n- {嘘|うそ}みたい: unbelievable, too good to be true\n- {嘘|うそ}でしょ: you're kidding, no way",
